<title>USA: Glickman, Barshefsky at Senate Ag panel April 24.</title>
<headline>Glickman, Barshefsky at Senate Ag panel April 24.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-04-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Secretary of Agriculture Dan Glickman and U.S. Trade Representative Charlene Barshefsky will testify April 24 at 0900 EST before the Senate Agriculture Committee on the opportunities for U.S. farm exports, Sen. Richard Lugar (R-Ind), chairman of the committee, announced Monday.</p>
<p>Lugar has introduced legislation to give the president fast-track trading authority and has asked the administration to keep agriculture at the center of global trade talks.</p>
<p>He said barriers to agricultural trade distort the markets and should be reduced.</p>
</text>
